Maintainer: Max Anjos <maxanjos@campus.ul.pt>
Description: Tools for analysing and visualising Local Climate Zones (LCZ)
    and urban heat islands at multiple spatial and temporal resolutions.
    Provides functions to retrieve LCZ maps from global, European and
    continental United States datasets and from the 'LCZ Generator',
    compute LCZ areas and urban canopy parameters, and combine LCZ maps with
    air temperature observations to analyse time series, thermal anomalies
    and urban heat island intensity, and to produce and evaluate LCZ-based
    kriging interpolation maps. Methods follow Stewart and Oke (2012)
    <doi:10.1175/BAMS-D-11-00019.1> and Demuzere et al. (2022)
    <doi:10.5194/essd-14-3835-2022>.
